{
  "about": "Frame vectors for every codec of the control socket's wire (the desktop's Rust proxy is the next one). A frame is a 4-byte big-endian unsigned length, then that many bytes of UTF-8 JSON holding one object (core/recursion_core/control_transport/framing.py at master_head). Bodies are written with no spaces (separators ',' and ':'), non-ASCII as UTF-8, keys in the order given, and no NaN or Infinity. Every vector here is checked against that module by desktop/tests/check_codec.py. The desktop sends integers only, so no vector pins how a float is written. 'generated' bodies are described, not stored: '{\"op\":\"control\",\"method\":\"run.start\",\"params\":{\"prompt\":\"' + 'a' * n + '\"}}' with n chosen so the body has exactly body_bytes bytes.",
  "master_head": "fb578e31a2c0469457a23dbcaa4030bdd24cef64",
  "max_frame_bytes": 1048576,
